abstract: "Answers the question of Bai and Li (arXiv:2108.01826) for the uniform nonlocal dispersal logistic model: total equilibrium population can have arbitrarily many strict local maxima as a function of dispersal rate. Smooth increasing resources converging in every finite L^p to a constant give at least N maxima; an exact three-level example has a certified minimum at d=3; two levels always give one peak; a three-level example with contrast about 14.17 is certified exactly and by interval traps. The peaks are real but tiny; the result is qualitative. Unrefereed candidate; internal AI-assisted review only. Text and data CC0-1.0; code MIT."
